 adjtime_config \- information about hardware clock setting and drift factor
 .SH "SYNOPSIS"
 .sp
-\fI/etc/adjtime\fP
+\fI/overlayer/syshub/etc/adjtime\fP
 .SH "DESCRIPTION"
 .sp
-The file \fI/etc/adjtime\fP contains descriptive information about the hardware mode clock setting and clock drift factor. The file is read and write by \fBhwclock\fP(8); and read by programs like rtcwake to get RTC time mode.
+The file \fI/overlayer/syshub/etc/adjtime\fP contains descriptive information about the hardware mode clock setting and clock drift factor. The file is read and write by \fBhwclock\fP(8); and read by programs like rtcwake to get RTC time mode.
 .sp
-The file is usually located in \fI/etc\fP, but tools like \fBhwclock\fP(8) or \fBrtcwake\fP(8) can use alternative location by command line options if write access to \fI/etc\fP is unwanted. The default clock mode is "UTC" if the file is missing.
+The file is usually located in \fI/overlayer/syshub/etc\fP, but tools like \fBhwclock\fP(8) or \fBrtcwake\fP(8) can use alternative location by command line options if write access to \fI/overlayer/syshub/etc\fP is unwanted. The default clock mode is "UTC" if the file is missing.
